# Per-node API keys for deploy/docker-compose.yml (L-03, L-08).
#
# `deploy/mesh-init.sh` creates `deploy/.env` with fresh keys when there is
# none, and also prepares the mesh the stack needs — run it before the first
# `up` (README, "Multi-node stack"). To choose the keys yourself, copy this file
# to `deploy/.env` and replace every value first; Compose reads a `.env` next to
# the compose file automatically, so no keys go on the command line or into
# your shell history.
#
# `deploy/.env` must NOT be committed. The repository `.gitignore` already
# ignores `.env`; this `.env.example` is the committed template and carries no
# secret.
#
# ── Generating values ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One key PER NODE, never one shared key: a shared key means compromising any
# single node hands the attacker write access to all three, and rotating it is
# an all-or-nothing outage.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# gl-node enforces a 16-byte minimum on `auth.apiKey` and refuses a denylist of
# published sample strings ("change-me", "changeme", "password", "secret", the
# README's placeholder, …) — matched case-insensitively on the trimmed value.
# A generated 64-character hex string satisfies both.
#
# ── The placeholders below fail closed BY CONSTRUCTION ───────────────────────
# They are 11 bytes, under the 16-byte floor, so a stack started with this file
# unedited dies at config validation naming `auth.apiKey` rather than coming up
# with a guessable credential. That is deliberate: three DISTINCT placeholders
# cannot all be denylist entries (the denylist matches exactly), so the length
# floor is what has to catch them. Do not "fix" the boot failure by padding
# these out — replace them.
#
# The environment value takes precedence over any non-empty `apiKey` in
# gl-node.docker.json, so rotation happens here and the node logs a warning
# whenever both are set.

GL_NODE_0_API_KEY=change-me-0
GL_NODE_1_API_KEY=change-me-1
GL_NODE_2_API_KEY=change-me-2
